# cargo's tree, which since DRAGON-590 also holds `target/artifacts/`: the ONE
# build-output directory, the same relative path on every platform, where each
# `just` recipe leaves its finished artifact plus the stable path a desktop
# shortcut points at. Covered by this line, nothing extra needed.
/target
# The container and cross-boot BUILD STATE, which deliberately stays OUT of
# target/ (see scripts/artifacts.sh for the full reasoning). These are scratch,
# not output: the finished artifact is moved into target/artifacts/ afterwards.
#   target-appimage/  the AppImage container's CARGO_HOME + CARGO_TARGET_DIR
#   target-dist/      the Rocky 9 shipping container's output mount (root-owned)
#   target-win/       the Windows boot's whole cargo tree (dual-boot shared tree)
#   target-mac/       cross-target mac CHECK artifacts (never a real build)
/target-appimage/
/target-dist/
/target-win/
/target-mac/
# Vendored static ffmpeg/ffprobe for the mac build, never committed (huge binaries).
/vendor/
# `mkdocs build` output for the documentation site (mkdocs.yml + site-src/).
# The built site is published by CI, never committed.
/site/
# A local virtualenv for previewing the docs site (`just docs`).
/.venv-docs/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak
dependencies.pdf

# transient perf-audit artifacts (see audit-recovery.md)
/audit.md
/audit-recovery.md
/audit/
